    "summary": "The Galmudug electoral commission announced that the Justice and Development Party (JSP) secured a majority in the region's parliamentary elections held in Dhusamareb.",
    "content": "The independent electoral commission for Galmudug announced the results of the region's parliamentary elections on Sunday in Dhusamareb. According to the commission, the Justice and Development Party (JSP) won a majority of the seats, positioning it to form the next regional government.\n\nThe elections, which were held under a clan-based power-sharing model, saw JSP emerge with the largest bloc in the regional assembly. The party, led by Ahmed Abdisalam Adan, campaigned on promises of improved security, economic development, and better public services. Other parties and independent candidates also secured seats, but none matched JSP's tally.\n\nThis election follows months of political tension in Galmudug, including disputes over the composition of the electoral commission and the timing of the vote. The federal government and international partners had urged a peaceful and transparent process, hoping to avoid the delays and violence that have marred previous regional elections.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the outcome is significant as Galmudug is a key region in central Somalia, and its stability affects broader national politics. Many diaspora members have invested in Galmudug and are closely watching the formation of the new administration, which will determine policies on security, taxation, and reconstruction. The JSP's majority may also influence the region's relationship with the federal government and its role in upcoming national elections.\n\nThe electoral commission has not yet released the full breakdown of seats, but officials from various parties have accepted the results and called for calm. The new parliament is expected to convene in the coming weeks to elect a speaker and regional president. The international community, including the United Nations, has welcomed the peaceful conduct of the vote and urged continued dialogue among all stakeholders.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/ururka-dowladda-ee-jsp-oo-ku-guulaystey-aqlibiyadda-doorashadii-galmudug/426149/",
