    "content": "The Speaker of Somalia's Federal Parliament, Abdulkadir Mohamed Nur (Jamac), chaired the 21st meeting of the Forum of Speakers of the East African Community (EAC) parliaments in Arusha, Tanzania, on October 2, 2026. The session brought together presiding officers from the regional bloc's member states.\n\nDiscussions centered on strengthening cooperation between the EAC's national assemblies, advancing parliamentary diplomacy, and exchanging institutional experience. Participants also examined ways to bring regional integration closer to citizens in member countries.\n\nNur's role as chair of the forum's speakers follows Somalia's admission to the EAC in 2023, a process that required the Federal Parliament to align domestic legislation with regional protocols. As chair, he is tasked with guiding the forum's agenda during a period in which the bloc is working to implement its customs union and common market arrangements.\n\nThe EAC Speakers' Forum serves as a consultative platform for legislative leaders rather than a decision-making body, but its recommendations often inform policy debates in member parliaments. Somalia's chairmanship gives Somali legislators a formal channel to raise priorities such as trade access, labor mobility, and security cooperation.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the Arusha meeting carries practical significance. Many diaspora businesses trade across East African markets, and EAC-level decisions on tariffs, movement of goods, and investment rules can affect those operations directly. Parliamentary coordination on such issues can help ensure that Somali commercial and community interests are considered as regional policy takes shape.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/02/guddoomiyaha-golaha-shacabka-oo-shir-guddoomiyey-kulanka-guddoonka-baarlamaannada-eac/",
