    "summary": "The Somali National AI Centre at Somali National University held a roundtable in Mogadishu to discuss building a strong foundation for AI and leveraging technological opportunities.",
    "content": "The Somali National AI Centre (SNAIC) at Somali National University (SNU) convened a roundtable discussion in Mogadishu on Wednesday, focusing on the future of artificial intelligence in Somalia and the need to establish a robust framework to harness AI-driven opportunities.\n\nThe event brought together representatives from universities, technology companies, and other organizations interested in advancing AI in the country. Participants exchanged views and recommendations on how Somalia could develop a comprehensive AI strategy, according to a report by Goobjoog.\n\nThe roundtable is part of broader efforts to promote AI research and innovation in Somalia. SNAIC, based at SNU, has been active in fostering dialogue among stakeholders to address the challenges and opportunities presented by AI.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the discussion holds particular significance. Many diaspora professionals work in technology and AI-related fields and can contribute expertise, investment, and partnerships to support Somalia's digital transformation. The outcomes of such gatherings may inform policies and initiatives that diaspora members can engage with.\n\nAs Somalia continues to rebuild its institutions, the role of emerging technologies like AI is increasingly seen as critical for economic growth and development. The roundtable reflects a growing recognition of the need for collaborative efforts to ensure the country is not left behind in the global AI race.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/02/xarunta-snaic-oo-qabatay-kulan-dood-cilmiyeed-looga-hadlay-mustaqbalka-garaad-gacmeedka-soomaaliya/",
